WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Good morning, John!

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.699
You were recently making fun of my new hairstyle.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:05.640
Which is fine, because we're brothers, and
that's what brothers do.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.290
But coming right back at you John, I gotta
say WHAT IS THIS?

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.290
WHAT?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.290
WHY?

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.639
Come on, we've been doing this for 8 years,
do you have no sense of composition?!

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.310
You gotta bunch of stuff on the wall over
here, nicely placed and visually interesting

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.019
without being distracting - AND THEN BWOM,
NOTHING.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.510
Blank space, baby.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.300
Help us John, help free us from the scourge
of the nothing, Artax is dead and you need

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.810
to name the childlike empress, BASTION, CALL
MY NAME!

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.050
Are the new viewers gone yet?

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.500
Some friends of mine, they have a YouTube
channel where they play board games while

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.500
being drunk.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.020
They play this improv game called "That's
not my name".

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.421
You know the song that this is based on, [singing]
They call me hell, they call me Janet, they

00:00:41.421 --> 00:00:43.930
call me Stacey, they call me Earl...

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:44.930
That song?

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.581
I don't know what the actual names are.

00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:49.721
The idea of the game is you go around in a
circle and you sing that song, with the "That's

00:00:49.721 --> 00:00:54.601
not my name / that's not my name" in it, and
then the next person has to do it and they

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:58.140
have to come up with different names to put
in, it's really fun.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.890
So if ever you're bored that's just a, it's
a fun thing to do, Katherine and I do it all

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:02.890
the time.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:08.210
[singing] They call me Brian, they call me
Nargle, the call me Amber, they call me Jeff,

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.210
that's not my name.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.210
None of those are my names.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.750
I used to think that butterflies were pretty
much just caterpillars that had had some modifications

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:14.750
made to them.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.710
But it turns out that caterpillars actually
just turn into this, like, liquid, soupy,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.650
organic goop inside of the cocoon and then
reform entirely into butterflies.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.060
And that's not even the weird part.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.881
The weird part is that caterpillars can be
taught to fear smells and then they turn into

00:01:26.881 --> 00:01:31.700
that goop, turn into butterflies, and the
butterflies remain afraid of those smells.

